<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n557" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Acrae</span></b> , ārum, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄκραι</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city of Sicily</i>, <i>on a lofty
				hill near Syracuse</i>, <i>now Palazzolo</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				24, 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 14, 206</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town in the Chersonesus Taurica</i> (Crimea),
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				4, 12, 26, § 86</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
